 "notes": [
  "The supplied part match (accel-adxl362) has SPI pins (VCC, GND, SCLK, MOSI...) that don't fit this analog breakout. I used the catalogue's adxl335 instead, whose ports ST, Z, Y, X, GND, VCC match the board in the circuit image.",
  "Pin mapping from the schematic and table: A0 to ST, A1 to Z, A2 to Y, A3 to X, A4 to GND, A5 to VDD (VCC). A4 is driven LOW and A5 HIGH in code to power the sensor.",
  "The breakout's 6 pins sit in breadboard columns 4-9, row j. In the image, row j is at the top of the board. I mapped rows f-j to bank 'b' per the catalogue. Each jumper wire lands in the same column strip, in a different row.",
  "The tutorial doesn't name its wire colours. The colours used are the ones in the circuit image."
 ],
